      "text": "The first digit has two possibilities: 2 or 9. For each of these possibilities, there are two choices for the second digit, 1/3 from 2 and 2/3 from 9. For each of these, there are three possibilities (remaining two) for the third digit, also determined from 2 or 9. For the last digit, only one possibility exists to maintain specificity of our number. Thus the total of possibilities is 2 x 1/3 x 2/3 x 3 x 1 = 4.\nThe answer is 4.",
